  "summary": "A standardized figure drawing method using a 9-head proportion system for fashion design.",
  "description": "The aesthetic features elongated, stylized figures with exaggerated proportions to showcase clothing designs; developed by fashion schools to standardize figure representation while allowing garment details to be clearly visible.",
  "culturalContext": "The croquis 9-head convention — fashion illustration's elongated figure standard — stretches the human body from realistic 7.5-8 heads to 9-10 for runway elegance: the figure drawn in standardized Croquis templates (bony landmarks, weight-shifted contrapposto) under watercolor-and-marker rendering culture (Anna Kiper, Bina Abling textbooks). Design rooms live by the croquis; the exaggerated silhouette communicates garment logic faster than photography.",
